      "writtenOn": "2024-09-27T02:47:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m having some second thoughts here. What if we changed the logic in `selinux_android_file_context_handle` to transparently do the caching? This would avoid adding a very similar function to the library.\n\nThe main drawback is that we are changing the behaviour of that function. I couldn\u0027t think about a blocking use-case here. Is there a process known to force the reloading of the file_contexts which relies on this behaviour? I don\u0027t think `init` does, nor does file_contexts in apexes, but I might be wrong?",
      "revId": "9f16e0318502adfc15afe68a0216a6b3090fd00f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b4bf559b_79ba68c5",
        "filename": "libselinux/include/selinux/android.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1561651
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-27T02:47:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should be able to mark this function as deprecated in favour of your new function. Could you add a comment here and reference the new function as the alternative? You can also include a warning that calling this function twice will reparse the configuration files and hence have a performance impact. Thanks!",
      "revId": "9f16e0318502adfc15afe68a0216a6b3090fd00f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
